commitments.text:
1. To establish long-term environmental monitoring stations that record: 
●     biweekly snow depth; 
●     minimum and maximum daily temperature; 
●     precipitation as rainfall 
to provide understanding of the natural variance in climatic variables important to ungulates.

2. To determine if changes in the annual migration and seasonal movements occur near the Tulsequah Chief Mine and Mine Access 
Road. Radio-telemetry and presence/absence surveys will be used to detect:
●     disruption of movement between summer and winter ranges; 
●     disruption of access to preferred calving grounds; 
●     behaviour responses to the road corridor.
